    <tags>bff-api, communication</tags>
    <rigor-hint>FULL</rigor-hint>
    <rigor-reason>Implements the confidence→status decision + auto-file behavior — the highest-consequence logic in the engine (an owner override of design DEC-4, ADR Tension Path A); gates auto-file behind an ADR-018 per-tenant kill-switch that must flip without redeploy; writes provenance JSON; respects ADR-018 / ADR-024 / ADR-045 + bff-extensions governance.</rigor-reason>
    <parallel-group>W1-status</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <fr-refs>FR-11</fr-refs>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <effort>xhigh</effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Implement the confidence→status ladder that maps aggregated engine `RungMatch` results (from rungs 0–3, tasks 012–014; later rungs 4–5 in W3) to `sprk_associationstatus`, and the auto-file behavior:

    • **≥0.85 AND deterministic (rungs 0–3 only)** → `Resolved` + **AUTO-FILE** (owner override of design DEC-4 — auto-file is ON at launch).
    • **0.50–0.85, OR ANY AI rung (4–5) involved** → `Suggested`.
    • **&lt;0.50 or no match** → `Pending Review`.
    • **conflicting high-confidence matches** → `Ambiguous`.

    Auto-file is gated by a per-tenant **ADR-018 kill-switch** (config, default-ON for deterministic ≥0.85) that flips the engine to suggest-only WITHOUT redeploy. **AI rungs NEVER auto-file** — even at high confidence they land as `Suggested`/`Ambiguous`. Write the full provenance (which rungs fired, per-attribute confidence, chosen status, auto-file decision) as JSON into `sprk_associationprovenance`.

    This is an ADR Tension Path A (project-scoped exception): auto-file-ON deviates from the design's conservative default, but stays within ADR-018's kill-switch guardrail and §5.4's ≥0.85→`Resolved` ladder. Misfile is re-file (audited), never delete.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Spaarke BFF engineer owning the association decision layer. Authority on `src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/`. Fluent in ADR-018 (kill-switch config; per-tenant enable/disable without redeploy), ADR-024 (regarding family), ADR-032 (Null-Object for feature-gated services), ADR-045 (Communication ADR), and `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md`. Understands this is a high-consequence, owner-overridden behavior (ADR Tension Path A) demanding careful, testable logic.
  </role>

  <goal>
    Aggregated engine results map to `sprk_associationstatus` via the ladder: deterministic ≥0.85 → `Resolved` + auto-file; 0.50–0.85 or any AI rung → `Suggested`; &lt;0.50/none → `Pending Review`; conflicting high → `Ambiguous`. Auto-file is governed by an ADR-018 per-tenant kill-switch (default-on for deterministic ≥0.85) that flips to suggest-only without redeploy. AI rungs never auto-file. Full provenance is persisted as JSON in `sprk_associationprovenance`. Build clean; ladder + kill-switch + AI-never-auto-file + provenance tests pass; publish-size + CVE + bff-extensions Placement Justification reported.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Rungs 0–3 (tasks 012–014) emit `RungMatch` results with per-attribute confidence + provenance. Task 015 is the decision layer that turns those into a status + an auto-file action. It is the single highest-consequence piece of Wave 1: auto-filing a communication to the wrong matter is a real risk, mitigated by (a) restricting auto-file to DETERMINISTIC rungs only, (b) the ≥0.85 threshold, (c) the ADR-018 per-tenant kill-switch escape hatch (flip to suggest-only, no redeploy), and (d) misfile = re-file (audited), never delete (R-1).

      Owner clarification (2026-07-14) + ADR Tension Path A: auto-file is ON at launch for deterministic ≥0.85 — a deliberate deviation from design DEC-4's "suggest-only first," within ADR-018's guardrail. This override is recorded in spec §ADR Tensions and CLAUDE.md.

      W0 task 002 adds the `Suggested`/`Ambiguous` option-set values (integers verified via Dataverse MCP) — this task depends on those existing. The `sprk_associationprovenance` JSON column is added in W0 task 001.

      AI rungs 4 (semantic, task 030) and 5 (LLM, task 031) land in W3 and MUST NEVER auto-file. Task 015's ladder must already encode "any AI rung ⇒ never `Resolved`/auto-file" so W3 needs no re-plumbing — it only registers higher rungs the ladder already treats as suggest-only.
    </background>
