  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">FR-11 ladder (exact): deterministic (rungs 0–3) ≥0.85 → `Resolved` + auto-file; 0.50–0.85 OR any AI rung → `Suggested`; &lt;0.50/none → `Pending Review`; conflicting high-confidence → `Ambiguous`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">AI rungs (4–5) NEVER auto-file — always `Suggested`/`Ambiguous`, regardless of score. Encode this now so W3 needs no ladder change.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-018">Auto-file gated by a per-tenant kill-switch (config, default-ON for deterministic ≥0.85) that flips to suggest-only WITHOUT redeploy. No recompile/redeploy to disable.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR Tension Path A">Auto-file-ON is a documented owner override of design DEC-4; stays within ADR-018 + §5.4 ladder. Misfile is re-file (audited), never delete (R-1).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Persist full provenance (rungs fired, per-attribute confidence, chosen status, auto-file decision + reason) as JSON in `sprk_associationprovenance`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Depends on W0 task 002 `Suggested`/`Ambiguous` option-set integers (verified via Dataverse MCP) and task 001 `sprk_associationprovenance` column.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-024">Auto-file writes typed regarding lookups + denormalized fields; no new regarding mechanism.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-032">If the kill-switch is modeled as a feature-gated service, use the Null-Object pattern so unconditionally-mapped consumers stay registered.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-045">Status ladder + kill-switch codified in ADR-045; confirm alignment.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">bff-extensions Placement Justification in the PR; publish-size delta (baseline ~49.63 MB incl. PDBs); no new HIGH CVE.</constraint>
  </constraints>

