  <steps>
    <step order="1">Read the task-011 engine contract + `RungMatch` aggregation; read `CommunicationStatus.cs` + confirm the W0 task-002 `Suggested`/`Ambiguous` option-set integers (via task-002 notes / Dataverse MCP) and the task-001 `sprk_associationprovenance` column.</step>
    <step order="2">Read ADR-018 + ADR-032 to design the per-tenant kill-switch (config source, per-tenant resolution, runtime flip; Null-Object if feature-gated).</step>
    <step order="3">Read `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md` §F/§F.1 + the ADR Tension Path A entry in `spec.md` so the auto-file override is implemented within its guardrail.</step>
    <step order="4">Implement the confidence→status mapper: aggregate rung results (max/combined confidence + rung provenance); classify per the exact ladder; flag "any AI rung present ⇒ never auto-file"; detect conflicting high-confidence matches → `Ambiguous`.</step>
    <step order="5">Implement the auto-file action for deterministic ≥0.85 → set `Resolved` + write regarding (ADR-024) — but ONLY when the ADR-018 per-tenant kill-switch is enabled; when disabled, downgrade to `Suggested` (suggest-only) without any code path change/redeploy.</step>
    <step order="6">Serialize full provenance (rungs fired, per-attribute confidence, chosen status, auto-file decision + reason incl. "kill-switch off ⇒ suggested") to JSON and persist to `sprk_associationprovenance`.</step>
    <step order="7">Wire the mapper into the engine/enrichment output so status + provenance are written for both inbound and outbound. Register any new service via `CommunicationModule` (unconditional / Null-Object per ADR-032).</step>
    <step order="8">Write tests covering: each ladder band; deterministic ≥0.85 auto-files to `Resolved`; kill-switch OFF ⇒ same match becomes `Suggested` (no redeploy); AI-rung match at ≥0.85 ⇒ `Suggested`/`Ambiguous`, NEVER auto-file; conflicting high ⇒ `Ambiguous`; provenance JSON shape. Seed fixtures across the ladder.</step>
    <step order="9">Run `dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/` + `dotnet test tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/ --filter Communication`; confirm rung tests (012–014) + task-011 characterization tests still pass.</step>
    <step order="9.1">Run `dotnet publish -c Release src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ -o c:/tmp/r4-015-publish/`; report compressed size + delta vs ~49.63 MB baseline. Expected ≈ 0.</step>
    <step order="9.2">Run `dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive` — confirm no new HIGH-severity CVEs.</step>
    <step order="9.5">FULL-rigor quality gates: `code-review` on the diff; `adr-check` against `spec.md` (focus FR-11 ladder + ADR-018 kill-switch + ADR Tension Path A + AI-never-auto-file). Address Critical findings; cite the ADR Tension Path A rationale + bff-extensions Placement Justification in the PR.</step>
    <step order="10">Run `/conflict-check` before the PR (BFF hot-path).</step>
    <step order="11">Update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md` (015 ✅) + `current-task.md`; unblock 030/051; record decisions (confidence-aggregation rule, conflict-detection heuristic, kill-switch config key, provenance schema).</step>
  </steps>

