  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Deterministic (rungs 0–3) match ≥0.85 → status `Resolved` + auto-file (regarding written) when kill-switch enabled.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Same deterministic ≥0.85 match with the ADR-018 per-tenant kill-switch DISABLED → `Suggested` (suggest-only), with no redeploy/code change (config flip only).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Match in 0.50–0.85, or ANY match involving an AI rung, → `Suggested`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">An AI-rung match at ≥0.85 is `Suggested`/`Ambiguous` and NEVER auto-files.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No match / &lt;0.50 → `Pending Review`; conflicting high-confidence matches → `Ambiguous`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Full provenance (rungs fired, per-attribute confidence, chosen status, auto-file decision + reason) is written as JSON to `sprk_associationprovenance`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`Suggested`/`Ambiguous` statuses use the W0 task-002 verified option-set integers (no collision).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Status + provenance are written identically for inbound and outbound (direction symmetry); rung + characterization tests still pass.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`dotnet build` clean; publish-size delta ≈ 0; no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
